  "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the first digit of the serial number of the part. Then the support is $S={2,3,4,5,6,7,8},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{7}:$\n\n$$\nf(2)=f(3)=\u2026=f(8)=\\frac{1}{7}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+\u2026+8\\cdot f(8) \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{7})+3(\\frac{1}{7})+\u2026+8(\\frac{1}{7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}+\\frac{3}{7}+\u2026+\\frac{8}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+3+4+5+6+7+8}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{7} \\\\  & =5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
